From 10d4989e2e53fb5eaf3c5fe32fbb218457ce6c7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AbhishekPok <abhishekpokhrel001@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:04:43 +0545
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Framework fixes for the mac-style shell: caches, faster
 lookups, audio, lock

- font: cache per-(font, letter) metrics, per-font metrics and glyph
  outline bounds; text measuring re-parsed font tables on every redraw
- fasthash: FxHash-style hasher for the service store, per-frame read
  sets and font caches; per-thread service lookup cache in store::find
- cli: build the user's shell crate at opt-level 2 (it was unoptimised)
- audio: an unreadable or zero-channel level keeps the last value instead
  of reporting 0%, which popped false volume HUDs
- lock: create lock surfaces right after requesting the lock; keep a lost
  output's pending lock surface alive; Lock::active()
- input: map clip rects through the target transform (scrolled settings)
- bluetooth: unblock rfkill and retry Powered
- run: write the shell's stderr to ~/.cache/amane/amane.log

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
