+ * hyprland destroys a lock surface on its own when the output goes away
+ * before the lock is granted (a monitor unplugged as the lid closes), without
+ * telling the client, so destroying it again is an "invalid object" that
+ * kills the shell and leaves the session locked with no lock screen. Once
+ * locked it keeps the surface instead, and nothing says which case this is,
+ * so a lock surface on a lost output is never destroyed: the gpu still lets
+ * go of it, and the compositor drops what is left with the lock
+ */
+fn close_on_lost_output(window: OpenWindow) {
